contentText:
Ella Langley continues heating up the Billboard Hot 100 as &#8220;Choosin&#8217; Texas&#8221; reigns for a 16th week, while her album Dandelion remains in the top 5 of the all-genre Billboard 200. Now, Langley is bringing a bit of that Dandelion vibe to a new collaboration with Shiner beer.

On Aug. 13, Shiner will launch the limited collaboration Dandelion Honey Kolsch, inspired by her album. The Kolsch-style beer is brewed with dandelion honey, offering sweet floral notes. The bottle is also inspired by the album, with its label featuring honey tones and emblazoned with dandelions.

Dandelion , Langley&#8217;s sophomore album, released in April and contains hits including &#8220;Choosin&#8217; Texas,&#8221; &#8220;Be Her,&#8221; and &#8220;Butterfly Season,&#8221; the latter featuring Miranda Lambert. Langley co-executive produced the album with Lambert and Ben West.

Shiner Beer teased the upcoming Langley collaboration with a video on Instagram, and was recently featured in a viral video clip of Langley from her video shoot for &#8220;Choosin&#8217; Texas.&#8221;

That viral clip featured Langley holding two bottles of Shiner beer, and then picking the bottom of one of the bottles with the heel of her boot, causing the cap to pop off. Langley then tilts a bottle toward the camera, nods and comments, &#8220;Cheers.&#8221;

Fans wanting to add more Ella vibes into their lifestyle have several ways to do so; Langley also recently teamed with NOYZ for the perfume Be Her By Ella Langley, a fragrance infused with notes of violet and peony. In recent months, she also teamed with BUM Energy for an energy drink and has collaborated with brands including American Eagle and Boot Barn .

As &#8220;Choosin&#8217; Texas&#8221; dominates for a 16th week, country songs also take the Billboard Hot 100&#8217;s entire top five spots, also including Morgan Wallen&#8217;s &#8220;Be By Now,&#8221; the Langley/Wallen collaboration &#8220;I Can&#8217;t Love You Anymore,&#8221; Taylor Swift&#8217;s &#8220;I Knew It, I Knew You&#8221; and Stella Lefty&#8217;s &#8220;Boston.&#8221;
